.TH GENESIS-RETINA 1 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-retina \- Genesis camera capture process (the eye)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgenesis\-retina\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesis-retina
is the standalone retinal process \(em the eye as its own organ. It
opens the V4L2 capture device named by
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
(default
.IR /dev/video0 )
and publishes raw frames into the POSIX shared-memory segment
.IR /genesis_optic_nerve ,
the canonical optic-nerve mapping read by both the daemon's
subcortical channels (SCN illuminance, collicular transients,
pretectal/pupil signals) and the cognitive mind's visual pathway.
.PP
It runs the same capture limb the daemon can embed
.RB ( OpticCapture )
\(em one implementation, two carriers. Camera ownership is settled
on the nerve itself, not by a flag: the daemon's own optic reader
watches the segment's frame counter, so while a retina publishes,
the daemon's embedded limb stays closed; if the retina dies the
daemon opens its limb and takes the camera. Exactly one process owns
the device at a time, and the eye heals in place.
.PP
It is built from
.I Self_World/src/bin/genesis-retina.rs
and is normally launched by
.BR genesis-cli (1)
before the daemon so the external eye wins the organ. It is not
supervised for respawn: a dead retina is covered by the daemon's
takeover, which keeps the camera for the daemon's life (a relaunched
retina then backs off on
.B EBUSY
and rests). Direct invocation is supported for diagnostics and
testing.
.PP
On SIGINT or SIGTERM the limb winds down and the segment's name is
unlinked, so a dead eye never publishes stale frames under a live
name. Readers already holding the mapping keep it until they detach.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
V4L2 device path to capture from (default
.IR /dev/video0 ).
When a non-default device is configured and fails to open, the limb
falls back to
.I /dev/video0
before accepting an absent eye entirely \(em sight is a degradation,
never a fault.
.TP
.B GENESIS_OPTIC_SEGMENT
Shared-memory segment name to publish (default
.IR /genesis_optic_nerve ).
Used by tests and diagnostic runs that need a private nerve.
.TP
.B GENESIS_DATA_DIR
Set by the launcher to bind the process to a Genesis instance; the
CLI validates identity through it when adopting or stopping.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /genesis_optic_nerve
POSIX shared-memory segment (in
.IR /dev/shm )
carrying the seqlock-style frame header plus RGB24 frame bytes.
RAM-backed; frames are streamed live and never persisted.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/genesis_retina.pid
PID file written by the launcher; used by
.B genesis --stop
and by startup adoption of a surviving process.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/retina.log
Capture log; rotated by the launcher at 5 MiB (two compressed
backups).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesis (1),
.BR genesis-cli (1),
.BR genesis-daemon (8),
.BR genesis-vision (7)
